--TEST--
`rule:types/decimal` and `rule:types/arithmetic`: `Core\Decimal`'s four cuts refuse at both of the type's bounds rather than narrowing to a scale that fits, and each names itself and the scale it was asked for
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The last scale a `decimal` holds, asked for from the side with no
// fractional digit of its own: 28 zeros fit in 96 bits.
echo Core\Decimal::floor(1, 28), "\n";

// ...and the first one it does not. Narrowing to 28 would make a cut a second
// inexact operation without saying so, which is the refusal the `*` and `/`
// rows already make.
try {
    echo Core\Decimal::floor(1.5, 29), "\n";
} catch (ArithmeticError $deep) {
    echo $deep->message, "\n";
}
try {
    echo Core\Decimal::ceil(1.5, 29), "\n";
} catch (ArithmeticError $up) {
    echo $up->message, "\n";
}

// The other bound, reached from the other side: a value with eleven digits
// before the point cannot carry 28 after it, because that is 10^38 and the
// mantissa is 96 bits.
try {
    echo Core\Decimal::truncate(10000000000, 28), "\n";
} catch (ArithmeticError $wide) {
    echo $wide->message, "\n";
}
try {
    echo Core\Decimal::round(10000000000, Core\RoundMode::HalfUp, 28), "\n";
} catch (ArithmeticError $rounded) {
    echo $rounded->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
1.0000000000000000000000000000
Core\Decimal::floor cannot answer 1.5 at scale 29: a `decimal` holds 28 fractional digits and a 96-bit mantissa
Core\Decimal::ceil cannot answer 1.5 at scale 29: a `decimal` holds 28 fractional digits and a 96-bit mantissa
Core\Decimal::truncate cannot answer 10000000000 at scale 28: a `decimal` holds 28 fractional digits and a 96-bit mantissa
Core\Decimal::round cannot answer 10000000000 at scale 28: a `decimal` holds 28 fractional digits and a 96-bit mantissa
